      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:4:3:212:37",
      "text": [
        " يَوْمُ الْأَضْحَى فِي الْيَوْمِ الَّذِي يُصَامُ فِيهِ وَ يَوْمُ الْعَاشُورَاءِ فِي الْيَوْمِ الَّذِي يُفْطَرُ فِيهِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Muhammad Bin Al Husayn, from Muhammad Bin Ismail, from Al Husayn Bin Muslim, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Al-Hassan<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘The day of the slaughter is among the days in which it is Fasted, and the day of Ashura is the day which it is not Fasted’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "37. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Muhammad ibn al-Husayn from Muhammad ibn ‘Isma‘il from al-Husayn ibn Muslim who has said the following: “Abu al-Hassan, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘The day of al-Adha’ can coincide with a day for fasting, and al-‘Ashura’ with a day which is not for fasting.’” (Please consult Fatwa about Hadith 37 of this Chapter) "
        ]
      }
    },
